      "message": "Mhm, I still think this is fragile, but as said, I currently don\u0027t have a better idea, and I guess in the worst case we\u0027ll just update depot_tools again if it breaks.\n\nThat said, this is a plain substring search over the entire siso help ninja output. It would false-positive on a hypothetical future flag like --namespace-separator or even descriptive help text containing \"-namespace\".\n\nA more robust check could look for the flag as a distinct token, maybe this works?\n\n```\nreturn any(\n    part in [\"-namespace\"]\n    for line in res.stdout.splitlines()\n    for part in line.split()\n)\n```",
